# Corresponding source

These binaries are built from **Tomacco @TOMACCO_VERSION@**, commit
@TOMACCO_COMMIT@.

Tomacco's own source code is licensed under GPL-2.0-or-later. The
distributed binaries are conveyed under GPL-3.0-or-later, because they include
Apache-2.0 components (see [THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md](../THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md)).
The text of the GPL version 3 is in `COPYING.GPL-3.0` next to this file; the
GPL version 2 is in [LICENSE](../LICENSE).

## Where to get it

The complete corresponding source for these binaries is offered with the
release at
<https://github.com/marselnenaj/tomacco/releases/tag/v@TOMACCO_VERSION@>:

- `tomacco-@TOMACCO_VERSION@-source.tar.gz`, with its SHA-256 beside it in
  a `.sha256` file: every file Tomacco tracks at the tag
  `v@TOMACCO_VERSION@`, with the build files (`CMakeLists.txt`, `Cargo.toml`,
  `Cargo.lock`, `build.rs`) and the installer (`install.py`);
- in the same tarball, under `vendor/`, every Rust crate the control program
  `tomaccoctl` is built from, vendored with `cargo vendor` at the versions
  `Cargo.lock` pins, including the SQLite amalgamation that `libsqlite3-sys`
  bundles, and the `.cargo/config.toml` that builds from them without a
  network;
- `SOURCE_RELEASE.md` at the top of the tarball, which lists what it does not
  hold, with where to get each: the upstream commits the recipes in
  `share/tomacco` fetch and build from.

The source stays available there for at least three years after the last
binaries of this release were distributed. If the link stops working, ask for
the source in the project's issue tracker
(<https://github.com/marselnenaj/tomacco/issues>); you get it at no more
than the cost of physically performing the transfer.

Qt and FFmpeg are not part of these binaries. The desktop links them from your
system, and your distribution provides their source. No iOS
engine, Apple software or other third-party program is distributed with
Tomacco, and the tarball holds no Apple data; the recipes in
`share/tomacco` download and build those on your machine from the
upstream sources they name, and you supply your own iOS restore image.
